cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite TRACE, cite the exact released version and formal source used."
title: "TRACE: A structural language for examining decisions and transitions under uncertainty"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Goodbody
    given-names: Mark
version: 0.2.7
date-released: 2026-08-05
repository-code: "https://github.com/markgoodbody-bit/TRACE"
url: "https://github.com/markgoodbody-bit/TRACE/blob/main/TRACE_FORMAL_SEED_v0_2_7.md"
abstract: >-
  TRACE is a typed structural-awareness grammar for examining decisions and
  transitions under uncertainty. It separates world, scene, map, action,
  transition, evidence, uncertainty, authority, correction, burden and residue
  without claiming moral authority, validation or permission to act.
keywords:
  - uncertainty
  - decision-making
  - typed graphs
  - causal modelling
  - AI safety
  - systems engineering
  - correction
  - accountability
